Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/50] Ambient pirates: attack players only while crime is on

Renn's ambient criminal events went after players while crime was off
(LowSecCriminalsAttackPlayers is on by default).  Now they only go
after players unprovoked while crime is on, and then as the high-sec
and low-sec settings say.  With crime off they still arrive at belts
with ambient miners and gates with ambient traffic, hunt those ships,
and shoot back at a player who shoots them, but they no longer come to
a grid just because a player is there, and a lock alone doesn't start
a fight.

/crime off also stops ambient CONCORD and navy patrols answering a
crime, and every ambient patrol or pirate lets go of the players and
drones it is fighting.

An ambient pirate's first attack only puts it on the criminal record
while crime is on, and again once that record is gone, so one already
fighting when crime is switched on is flagged too.
